.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PROC_NAMESPACE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm proc_namespace
.Nd add, remove or clear scheme namespace prefixes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn proc_namespace proc op prefix prefix_len
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
changes the scheme namespace of
.Fa proc ,
which is
.Dv SELF_PROC
or a process handle with the
.Dv ADMIN
right.
.Fa op
is one of
.Dv namespace::ADD ,
.Dv namespace::REMOVE
or
.Dv namespace::CLEAR
(1, 2 and 3).
.Pp
.Dv ADD
grants every scheme name starting with the
.Fa prefix
bytes.
The caller may only grant a prefix inside its own namespace; the root
administrative namespace may grant any valid prefix.
.Dv REMOVE
removes the prefix from new lookups and registrations; existing scheme-file
handles keep working.
.Dv CLEAR
removes all prefixes, not exact names.
Adding an existing prefix or removing an absent one succeeds.
.Pp
Child namespaces are subsets of their parent's namespace.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Zero on success; a negative
.Va errno
on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Fa proc
is not a live process handle.
.It Er EPERM
The caller lacks
.Dv ADMIN
or tries to grant outside its own namespace.
.It Er EINVAL
The operation or prefix is invalid.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr handle_revoke 2 ,
.Xr open 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1, contract C17.
